IMPORT prelude

-- Weights and Measures Act 1975 (Singapore) -- what "use for trade" covers (s 5), which units a trader may use (ss 6, 18, 40),
-- when a trade scale is lawful (s 7(2), s 40(3)), false or unjust instruments and the employee and 12-month defences (s 14),
-- short weight and short packages (s 19, with the s 2 definitions of non-standard and inadequate packages), the food evaporation
-- defence (s 21(3)), weighing in the buyer's presence (s 28A), the default exemptions from quantity orders (s 16(4)), entry by
-- inspectors (s 30(1)(c)), composition (s 33) and penalties (ss 29A(5), 35).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021), informal consolidation "version in force from
-- 28/11/2025", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/WMA1975.txt. The latest amendment annotated is Act 7 of 2025 wef
-- 28/11/2025 (the definition of "food"); Act 13 of 2025 wef 01/07/2025 moved administration to the Competition and Consumer
-- Commission of Singapore. SECTION NUMBERS FOLLOW THE BODY: the arrangement at the top of the deposit is one number out of step
-- from s 16 to s 28 (for example it lists "Short weight" as s 18; the body numbers it s 19, and s 35 cites it as s 19).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: every hawker, market stall, petrol pump and supermarket package in Singapore
-- is weighed or measured under it, and the shopper's protections against short weight are here. SCOPED to what a shopper or small
-- trader meets. Not encoded: standards and the Schedules' tables (s 4, Second Schedule), pattern approval (ss 8, 9), regulations
-- and Minister's orders (ss 10, 12, 16(1)-(3), 37, 38), stamp-tampering offences beyond their penalty (s 11), the quantity-order
-- offences (s 17), warranty and third-party defences (ss 20, 22, 23), most of s 21, documents and road-vehicle check-weighing
-- (ss 21A, 24-26), Authorised Verifiers (ss 7A, 29A) beyond their penalty, arrest and recall (ss 31, 31A), corporations (s 36),
-- and anything in subsidiary legislation (prescribed errors, prescribed instruments, s 40 transactions), none of which was read.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions (the skill was not loadable in this
-- session; the example rows were followed). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Weights and Measures Act 1975 -- trade`

§§ `5 -- use for trade`

-- s 5(1): "use for trade" means use in Singapore in connection with a transaction for money or money's worth (or a toll or duty),
-- where "(c) the transaction is by reference to quantity" (or states the quantity) and "(d) the use is for the purpose of the
-- determination or statement of that quantity". (2): not where the quantity is of goods "required for despatch to a destination
-- outside Singapore" and nothing passes but title and price. (3): any instrument "made available in Singapore for use by the public,
-- whether on payment or otherwise" is treated as in use for trade (for Part 3).
GIVEN `for a transaction for money or money's worth` IS A BOOLEAN, `the transaction is by reference to quantity` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `used to determine or state that quantity` IS A BOOLEAN, `goods for despatch abroad with only title and price passing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `made available for use by the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument is in use for trade` IF
        `made available for use by the public`
    OR  (    `for a transaction for money or money's worth`
         AND `the transaction is by reference to quantity`
         AND `used to determine or state that quantity`
         AND (NOT `goods for despatch abroad with only title and price passing`))

§§ `6, 18 and 40 -- lawful units`

-- s 6(1): "Subject to section 40, a person must not use for trade any unit of measurement ... which is not included in the First
-- Schedule." (2): "must not use the carat (metric) for trade except for the purposes of transactions in precious stones or pearls."
-- (5): (1) does not apply to "the prescribing of, or the dispensing of a prescription for, health or medicinal products".
-- First Schedule: metric units only (kilometre ... millimetre; hectare, are, square metre ...; cubic metre ...; litre ...; tonne,
-- quintal, kilogram, hectogram, gram, carat (metric), milligram). Third Schedule: the customary hoon, chee, tahil and kati
-- ("16 Tahils = 1 Kati ... = 0.6048 kilogram"), lawful only in transactions prescribed by regulations under s 40(1), which applies
-- "despite anything in this Act". s 18(1) separately makes it an offence to deal, use or advertise in non-metric units.
DECLARE Unit IS ONE OF
    `kilogram`
    `gram`
    `litre`
    `metre`
    `square metre`
    `carat (metric)`
    `kati`
    `tahil`
    `pound`
    `foot`
    `gallon`

GIVEN `the unit` IS A Unit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unit is in the First Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the unit`
    WHEN `kati` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `tahil` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `pound` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `foot` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `gallon` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the unit` IS A Unit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unit is customary under the Third Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the unit`
    WHEN `kati` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `tahil` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the unit` IS A Unit, `dealing in precious stones or pearls` IS A BOOLEAN, `a transaction prescribed under s 40` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `prescribing or dispensing a health or medicinal product` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unit may be used for trade` IF
    IF `the unit` EQUALS `carat (metric)`
    THEN `dealing in precious stones or pearls`
    ELSE     `the unit is in the First Schedule` `the unit`
         OR  `prescribing or dispensing a health or medicinal product`
         OR  (`the unit is customary under the Third Schedule` `the unit` AND `a transaction prescribed under s 40`)

-- s 18(1)(d): an offence to use, "on any package, or in any price list or advertisement or otherwise, any unit ... other than a
-- weight or measure of the metric system, in advertising, displaying, or exposing goods for sale". (2): not for goods displayed for
-- sale BY RETAIL if "(a) that unit is additional to a unit ... of the metric system; and (b) that unit, the figures ... and the
-- numerical value of that unit are marked no larger than those of that metric weight or measure".
GIVEN `a non-metric unit is shown` IS A BOOLEAN, `goods displayed for sale by retail` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a metric unit is also shown` IS A BOOLEAN, `the non-metric marking is no larger` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the non-metric display is an offence` IF
        `a non-metric unit is shown`
    AND (NOT (`goods displayed for sale by retail` AND `a metric unit is also shown` AND `the non-metric marking is no larger`))

§§ `7(2) and 40(3) -- a lawful trade instrument`

-- s 7(2): for prescribed instruments, a person must not supply, use or possess for use for trade any instrument unless "(c) the
-- instrument has been submitted to and passed as being fit for such use by an Authorised Verifier ... or an inspector" and "(d) ...
-- affixed with (i) a stamp; and (ii) an Accuracy Label ... and both the stamp and Accuracy Label remain undefaced otherwise than by
-- reason of fair wear and tear". (Regulations under s 10 may provide otherwise; not modelled.) (3): offence, and forfeiture.
-- s 40(3)(a): an instrument in lawful trade use immediately before 1 January 2006 may continue "even though it does not have an
-- Accuracy Label affixed to it".
GIVEN `the instrument is of a prescribed class` IS A BOOLEAN, `passed as fit` IS A BOOLEAN, `stamped` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `bears an Accuracy Label` IS A BOOLEAN, `defaced beyond fair wear and tear` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `lawfully in trade use before 1 January 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument may be used for trade` IF
        (NOT `the instrument is of a prescribed class`)
    OR  (    `passed as fit`
         AND `stamped`
         AND (`bears an Accuracy Label` OR `lawfully in trade use before 1 January 2006`)
         AND (NOT `defaced beyond fair wear and tear`))

§§ `14 and 15 -- false or unjust instruments`

-- s 14(1): using for trade, or possessing for use for trade, an instrument "which is false or unjust" is an offence (strict on its
-- face). (2) defences: (a) "used the instrument only in the course of his or her employment by some other person" and "neither knew,
-- nor had any reason to suspect" it was false; or (b) the use or possession "took place during a period of 12 months immediately
-- following the month in which an Accuracy Label for the instrument was issued" and the same lack of knowledge.
-- s 15: an instrument found with a person carrying on trade, or on trade premises, is deemed possessed for use for trade "unless the
-- contrary is proved".
--
-- Months are counted as consecutive integers (year times 12 plus month). On the literal words, the window is the 12 months
-- FOLLOWING the month of issue, so use in the month of issue itself is outside defence (b). That is a literal reading, not a ruling.
GIVEN `the month the label was issued` IS A NUMBER, `the month of use` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use is within the 12 months following the label month` IF
        `the month of use` GREATER THAN `the month the label was issued`
    AND `the month of use` AT MOST `the month the label was issued` PLUS 12

GIVEN `found with a trader or on trade premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument is deemed possessed for use for trade` IF
    `found with a trader or on trade premises` AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`)

GIVEN `the instrument is false or unjust` IS A BOOLEAN, `used only as someone's employee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or had reason to suspect` IS A BOOLEAN, `the month the label was issued` IS A NUMBER, `the month of use` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the false instrument offence is made out` IF
        `the instrument is false or unjust`
    AND (NOT (    (NOT `knew or had reason to suspect`)
              AND (   `used only as someone's employee`
                   OR `the use is within the 12 months following the label month` `the month the label was issued` `the month of use`)))

§§ `2 and 19 -- short weight and short packages`

-- s 2(1): "non-standard package" -- contains less than the stated quantity "where the deficiency is more than the amount of error
-- prescribed ... but not more than twice that prescribed amount of error"; "inadequate package" -- "where the deficiency is more than
-- twice the amount of error prescribed". The Act does not name a package short by no more than the prescribed error; the label
-- `short within the prescribed error` below is the encoder's.
DECLARE PackageClass IS ONE OF
    `not short`
    `short within the prescribed error`
    `non-standard`
    `inadequate`

GIVEN `the deficiency` IS A NUMBER, `the prescribed error` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A PackageClass
`the class of a short package` MEANS
    IF `the deficiency` AT MOST `the prescribed error` THEN `short within the prescribed error`
    ELSE IF `the deficiency` AT MOST `the prescribed error` TIMES 2 THEN `non-standard` ELSE `inadequate`

GIVEN `the stated quantity` IS A NUMBER, `the actual quantity` IS A NUMBER, `the prescribed error` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A PackageClass
`the package class` MEANS
    IF `the actual quantity` AT LEAST `the stated quantity` THEN `not short`
    ELSE `the class of a short package` (`the stated quantity` MINUS `the actual quantity`) `the prescribed error`

-- s 19(1): "in selling or purporting to sell any goods by weight or other measurement or by number, delivers ... a lesser quantity
-- than that purported to be sold or than corresponds with the price charged" -- offence.
-- s 19(3): selling, offering or possessing for sale goods in a package that states its quantity is an offence "if the weight,
-- measure or number of the goods in the package is less than that stated". (4): "goods" includes catch weight goods. (5): for goods
-- OTHER THAN catch weight goods, the contents are deemed equal to the statement if the package, or its lot of packages, "meets the
-- conditions prescribed by regulations made under section 37" (not retrieved; a flag here).
-- s 19(8): nothing in s 19 applies to the s 16(4)(a) or (b) cases (armed forces goods; buyer's written notice of export or ship's
-- stores), nor, with exceptions, to sales for industrial or constructional use.
GIVEN `the quantity delivered` IS A NUMBER, `the quantity purported to be sold` IS A NUMBER, `the quantity the price pays for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the delivery is short weight` IF
        `the quantity delivered` LESS THAN `the quantity purported to be sold`
    OR  `the quantity delivered` LESS THAN `the quantity the price pays for`

GIVEN `the stated quantity` IS A NUMBER, `the actual quantity` IS A NUMBER, `catch weight goods` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the package or its lot meets the prescribed conditions` IS A BOOLEAN, `outside s 19 under s 19(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the short package offence is made out` IF
        `the actual quantity` LESS THAN `the stated quantity`
    AND (NOT ((NOT `catch weight goods`) AND `the package or its lot meets the prescribed conditions`))
    AND (NOT `outside s 19 under s 19(8)`)

-- s 19(6): defence for a package from a lot of DESICCATING goods: (a) at any time "on the day the package was made up or during a
-- period of 7 days beginning on the day after" -- the weighed average of a sample at least equalled the stated quantity, the number
-- of non-standard packages in the sample was within the number prescribed, and "there were no inadequate packages" in the sample;
-- or (b) at any time after that period, a sample "contained no inadequate packages". Day 0 below is the day of make-up.
GIVEN `days after make-up when sampled` IS A NUMBER, `the sample average at least the stated quantity` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `non-standard packages in the sample` IS A NUMBER, `the prescribed number of non-standard packages` IS A NUMBER,
      `inadequate packages in the sample` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the desiccating goods defence succeeds` IF
    IF `days after make-up when sampled` AT MOST 7
    THEN     `the sample average at least the stated quantity`
         AND `non-standard packages in the sample` AT MOST `the prescribed number of non-standard packages`
         AND `inadequate packages in the sample` EQUALS 0
    ELSE `inadequate packages in the sample` EQUALS 0

-- s 19(7): "any statement, whether oral or in writing, as to the weight of any goods is deemed, unless otherwise expressed, to be a
-- statement as to the net weight of the goods."
DECLARE WeightBasis IS ONE OF `net weight`, `gross weight`

GIVEN `gross weight was expressly stated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A WeightBasis
`the weight statement is read as` MEANS
    IF `gross weight was expressly stated` THEN `gross weight` ELSE `net weight`

§§ `21(3) -- evaporation and drainage of food`

-- s 21(3): on a retail sale of food "not being food prepacked in a container which is, or is required by this Act to be, marked with
-- an indication of quantity", a defence to prove "the deficiency was due wholly to unavoidable evaporation or drainage since the
-- sale and that due care and precaution were taken to minimise" it.
GIVEN `a retail sale of food` IS A BOOLEAN, `prepacked in a container marked or required to be marked with quantity` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `wholly due to unavoidable evaporation or drainage since the sale` IS A BOOLEAN, `due care was taken to minimise it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the evaporation defence succeeds` IF
        `a retail sale of food`
    AND (NOT `prepacked in a container marked or required to be marked with quantity`)
    AND `wholly due to unavoidable evaporation or drainage since the sale`
    AND `due care was taken to minimise it`

§§ `16(4) and 19(8) -- which sales the quantity rules reach`

-- s 16(4): until an order provides otherwise, exempt from "all such requirements" (the quantity orders under s 16): (a) goods for
-- the Singapore Armed Forces or a visiting force; (b) sales where the buyer gives written notice before completion that the goods
-- are for despatch abroad or ship's or aircraft stores; (c) goods sold "only for, use or consumption at the premises of the seller";
-- (d) food "prepacked together for consumption together as a meal and ready for such consumption without being cooked, heated or
-- otherwise prepared". s 19(8)(a) carries over only (a) and (b) to the short-weight offences.
DECLARE Sale IS ONE OF
    `goods for the armed forces`
    `goods bought for export on written notice`
    `food eaten at the seller's premises`
    `a prepacked ready-to-eat meal`
    `an ordinary retail sale`

GIVEN `the sale` IS A Sale
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `exempt from s 16 quantity orders by default` IF
    CONSIDER `the sale`
    WHEN `an ordinary retail sale` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the sale` IS A Sale
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the short weight rules of s 19 apply` IF
    CONSIDER `the sale`
    WHEN `goods for the armed forces` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `goods bought for export on written notice` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `28A -- weighing in the buyer's presence`

-- s 28A(1): goods offered for sale by retail by weight, measure or number "which are not prepackaged" must be weighed, measured or
-- counted "(a) at the time of sale; (b) in the presence of the buyer; and (c) in the case of goods sold by weight or measure, by
-- means of a suitable weighing or measuring instrument". (2): goods "prepackaged and weighed ... before they are so offered or
-- exposed for sale at the premises or place where they are so offered" must, "at the buyer's request", be weighed in the buyer's
-- presence by a suitable instrument. (3): the instrument must be placed so the weighing and reading "can be easily seen by the
-- buyer". (4): offence. The encoder reads (2) as goods weighed at the selling premises; the words allow that reading but are not
-- unambiguous. Prepackaged goods weighed elsewhere are not reached by s 28A on that reading.
GIVEN `prepackaged` IS A BOOLEAN, `weighed beforehand at the selling premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `the buyer asked` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `sold by number only` IS A BOOLEAN, `weighed at the time of sale` IS A BOOLEAN, `weighed in the buyer's presence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `on a suitable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN, `easily seen by the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seller complies with s 28A` IF
        (    (NOT `prepackaged`)
         AND `weighed at the time of sale`
         AND `weighed in the buyer's presence`
         AND (`sold by number only` OR `on a suitable instrument`)
         AND `easily seen by the buyer`)
    OR  (    `prepackaged`
         AND (NOT (`weighed beforehand at the selling premises` AND `the buyer asked`)))
    OR  (    `prepackaged`
         AND `weighed in the buyer's presence`
         AND (`sold by number only` OR `on a suitable instrument`)
         AND `easily seen by the buyer`)

§§ `30(1)(c) -- entry`

-- s 30(1)(c): an inspector or police officer may at all reasonable times "enter any premises at which he or she has reasonable cause
-- to believe there to be any such instrument or goods, not being premises used only as a private dwelling house".
GIVEN `reasonable cause to believe instruments or goods are there` IS A BOOLEAN, `used only as a private dwelling house` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an inspector may enter under s 30` IF
    `reasonable cause to believe instruments or goods are there` AND (NOT `used only as a private dwelling house`)

§§ `29A(5), 33 and 35 -- penalties`

-- s 35(1): an offence "under section 11(1), 11(3), 14(1), 14(3), 19(1), 19(2) or 32(1)" -- fine up to $5,000 or imprisonment up to
-- 3 months or both. (2): "any provision of this Act other than those mentioned in subsection (1)" -- fine up to $2,000.
-- s 29A(5) sets its own penalty for acting as an unappointed Authorised Verifier or using a false working standard: up to $10,000
-- or 2 years or both (s 29A(7) the same for an Authorised Verifier who fails an inspector's requirement). The encoder treats that
-- specific penalty as displacing s 35(2); s 35 does not say so (an inference).
-- s 33(1): the Controller may compound "any offence" for "a sum not exceeding $2,000".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `tampering with a stamp or Accuracy Label`
    `using a false or unjust instrument`
    `fraud in using an instrument`
    `delivering short weight`
    `misrepresenting quantity`
    `obstructing an inspector`
    `selling a package short of its stated quantity`
    `not weighing in the buyer's presence`
    `using an unlawful unit`
    `using an unstamped instrument`
    `trading in non-metric units`
    `acting as an unappointed Authorised Verifier`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is listed in s 35(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `tampering with a stamp or Accuracy Label` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `using a false or unjust instrument` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `fraud in using an instrument` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `delivering short weight` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `misrepresenting quantity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `obstructing an inspector` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `the offence` EQUALS `acting as an unappointed Authorised Verifier` THEN 10000
    ELSE IF `the offence is listed in s 35(1)` `the offence` THEN 5000 ELSE 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF `the offence` EQUALS `acting as an unappointed Authorised Verifier` THEN 24
    ELSE IF `the offence is listed in s 35(1)` `the offence` THEN 3 ELSE 0

GIVEN `the sum offered` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sum is within the composition limit` IF
    `the sum offered` AT MOST 2000
